WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.368 --> 00:00:02.702
-My first guest
is a very talented actor

00:00:02.702 --> 00:00:05.238
and one of the founders
of HITRECORD.

00:00:05.238 --> 00:00:08.574
Season 2 of his Emmy-winning
series "Create Together"

00:00:08.574 --> 00:00:11.644
premieres on YouTube
on April 22nd.

00:00:11.644 --> 00:00:15.448
Here is Joseph Gordon-Levitt!

00:00:15.448 --> 00:00:18.417
That's what I'm talking about.
Look! Come on, now.

00:00:18.417 --> 00:00:20.119
That's how you do it.

00:00:20.119 --> 00:00:22.155
-What's going on, man?
-I'm so happy you're back.

00:00:22.155 --> 00:00:24.456
Thank you for coming
back to the show, bud.

00:00:24.456 --> 00:00:26.392
-Always good to be here.
Thank you.

00:00:26.392 --> 00:00:28.560
-You're coming all the way
from New Zealand,

00:00:28.560 --> 00:00:29.695
so I appreciate that.

00:00:29.695 --> 00:00:31.297
What time is it there?

00:00:31.297 --> 00:00:34.066
-It's the morning. I just
dropped off my boy at school.

00:00:34.066 --> 00:00:35.201
-No way.

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:37.003
-Tomorrow morning.
I'm living in the future.

00:00:37.003 --> 00:00:39.205
-Wow. What's it like in the
future?

00:00:39.205 --> 00:00:43.109
-Man, it's good. I got to
tell you, I feel just so lucky.

00:00:43.109 --> 00:00:45.110
I almost feel guilty
talking about it sometimes,

00:00:45.110 --> 00:00:47.046
'cause if you don't know,

00:00:47.046 --> 00:00:49.549
New Zealand's one of like
only two countries in the world

00:00:49.549 --> 00:00:52.018
that's just contained
the pandemic.

00:00:52.018 --> 00:00:54.120
There aren't cases here.

00:00:54.120 --> 00:00:56.422
And I came here for work,
luckily.

00:00:56.422 --> 00:01:00.159
And it's hard.
You know, obviously,

00:01:00.159 --> 00:01:02.395
so much of the world is
going through such a hard time,

00:01:02.395 --> 00:01:04.597
and people are
getting sick and dying,

00:01:04.597 --> 00:01:06.032
and here we are,

00:01:06.032 --> 00:01:08.100
and I get to go to work
every day and not wear a mask.

00:01:08.100 --> 00:01:10.136
Like I said, I just
dropped my boy off at school.

00:01:10.136 --> 00:01:12.438
Like, I feel really lucky.

00:01:12.438 --> 00:01:15.808
But I honestly have to hand it
to the people of this country.

00:01:15.808 --> 00:01:18.310
They have an amazing leader,
Jacinda Ardern,

00:01:18.310 --> 00:01:20.113
which, by the way, I don't think
it's a coincidence

00:01:20.113 --> 00:01:23.016
that, you know, the country
led by a woman handled it.

00:01:23.016 --> 00:01:25.218
And also --
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:25.218 --> 00:01:26.953
Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:01:26.953 --> 00:01:29.955
-Yeah. I want to wish you
a happy belated birthday.

00:01:29.955 --> 00:01:31.190
Since I last talked you,

00:01:31.190 --> 00:01:32.891
you turned 40.
-Thanks, man.

00:01:32.891 --> 00:01:34.560
-40's a big deal!
Happy birthday!

00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:36.395
-I know. [ Chuckles ]

00:01:36.395 --> 00:01:39.732
-How does 40 feel to you?

00:01:39.732 --> 00:01:41.066
-I love it, man.

00:01:41.066 --> 00:01:43.769
I'm definitely happier
in my 40s than I've ever been.

00:01:43.769 --> 00:01:46.438
I mean, I've only been in my 40s
for a few months now.

00:01:46.438 --> 00:01:48.641
But, you know, growing up,

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:50.576
when I was young, I always
just wanted to be older.

00:01:50.576 --> 00:01:53.847
Like, I always felt like
I looked too young or I was --

00:01:53.847 --> 00:01:56.816
I looked like a kid, so people
wouldn't take me seriously.

00:01:56.816 --> 00:02:00.586
Actually, my wife was just
talking to a friend of hers,

00:02:00.586 --> 00:02:03.322
and her friend was like,

00:02:03.322 --> 00:02:05.824
"Oh, I just saw Joe
in this movie on TV.

00:02:05.824 --> 00:02:07.693
It was this really cute movie."

00:02:07.693 --> 00:02:08.928
My wife was like,
"Oh, what was it?"

00:02:08.928 --> 00:02:10.796
And she was like,
"I don't know. He was young.

00:02:10.796 --> 00:02:13.366
He was probably like,
I don't know, 10 or 11

00:02:13.366 --> 00:02:15.801
or something like that.
What was it?"

00:02:15.801 --> 00:02:19.205
And it turned out the movie was
"10 Things I Hate About You."

00:02:19.205 --> 00:02:21.874
Which, you know,
I was 17 in that movie.

00:02:21.874 --> 00:02:23.042
[ Laughter ]

00:02:23.042 --> 00:02:24.978
And my wife's friend
thought I was --

00:02:24.978 --> 00:02:27.313
literally thought
I was 10 or 11 in it.

00:02:27.313 --> 00:02:30.249
-I do want to show
baby Joseph Gordon-Levitt,

00:02:30.249 --> 00:02:31.317
'cause you posted this.

00:02:31.317 --> 00:02:34.087
You've been acting
for over 30 years.

00:02:34.087 --> 00:02:36.422
Here's you,
one of your first gigs.

00:02:36.422 --> 00:02:37.890
[ Audience awws ]
I mean, stop it.

00:02:37.890 --> 00:02:39.692
What a cute kid. Come on.

00:02:39.692 --> 00:02:42.328
Here you are. You're 17 here.

00:02:42.328 --> 00:02:43.429
And --

00:02:43.429 --> 00:02:46.265
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.265 --> 00:02:48.267
But you play --
You were 7 years old,

00:02:48.267 --> 00:02:51.671
and you played Bully #2
on "Family Ties."

00:02:51.671 --> 00:02:53.239
That's a breakout role.

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:55.174
What do you remember
from Bully #2?

00:02:55.174 --> 00:02:56.508
-If you don't remember,

00:02:56.508 --> 00:02:59.845
"Family Ties" was where
Michael J. Fox really broke out,

00:02:59.845 --> 00:03:01.280
and then he did
"Back to the Future,"

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:03.249
and then, you know, he became
Michael J. Fox.

00:03:03.249 --> 00:03:06.486
But I remember we all just
looked up to him so much,

00:03:06.486 --> 00:03:09.054
this whole classroom
full of young actors.

00:03:09.054 --> 00:03:10.056
-Oh, yeah.

00:03:10.056 --> 00:03:12.258
-And he could have
easily not cared.

00:03:12.258 --> 00:03:15.528
But he did.
He took the time to talk to us

00:03:15.528 --> 00:03:18.264
and encourage us
and be really positive with us.

00:03:18.264 --> 00:03:20.899
And I actually
got to see him again,

00:03:20.899 --> 00:03:23.068
you know, all these years later

00:03:23.068 --> 00:03:26.506
and man-to-man, say, like,

00:03:26.506 --> 00:03:29.275
"Dude, I was 7 on your set,

00:03:29.275 --> 00:03:30.776
and you made a difference to me.

00:03:30.776 --> 00:03:33.812
Like, you inspired me
and encouraged me,

00:03:33.812 --> 00:03:36.749
and you showed that, like,
an actor on a set can --

00:03:36.749 --> 00:03:39.118
doesn't have to be,
like, a stuck-up actor

00:03:39.118 --> 00:03:43.289
but can be a down-to-earth,
positive guy with kids

00:03:43.289 --> 00:03:44.690
who has time for everybody."

00:03:44.690 --> 00:03:47.160
And it meant a lot,
and I still remember it.

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:50.062
And he's just the sweetest guy,
Michael J. Fox.

00:03:50.062 --> 00:03:52.431
-Go Michael J. Fox.
I love that story.

00:03:52.431 --> 00:03:55.401
Thank you for telling
that story. That's awesome.

00:03:55.401 --> 00:04:00.473
Buddy, I love talking about
HITRECORD because it's --

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:02.909
-You were like the first
supporter of HITRECORD, man.

00:04:02.909 --> 00:04:04.143
I've been doing this
a long time,

00:04:04.143 --> 00:04:05.778
and you were always
so supportive.

00:04:05.778 --> 00:04:07.246
I really appreciate it.

00:04:07.246 --> 00:04:10.416
-Cut to last year,
you do a limited --

00:04:10.416 --> 00:04:13.519
You do a series called "Create
Together," a YouTube series,

00:04:13.519 --> 00:04:15.888
and it wins an Emmy.

00:04:15.888 --> 00:04:17.256
Congratulations, dude.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:17.256 --> 00:04:18.557
-Thanks, man.

00:04:18.557 --> 00:04:20.859
-Can we explain to folks,
like, how it works

00:04:20.859 --> 00:04:23.829
or how did you come up,
even, with the YouTube show?

00:04:23.829 --> 00:04:27.066
-HITRECORD is just a place
where people do exactly that.

00:04:27.066 --> 00:04:28.968
They create things together,
art of all kinds,

00:04:28.968 --> 00:04:31.203
short films or music
or writing or anything.

00:04:31.203 --> 00:04:34.707
And, you know, so much of online
art and creativity can be about,

00:04:34.707 --> 00:04:37.209
"Hey, world, look at me.
Look what I made."

00:04:37.209 --> 00:04:39.745
And that's great.

00:04:39.745 --> 00:04:41.647
But on HITRECORD,
it's less about, "Look at me,"

00:04:41.647 --> 00:04:44.316
and it's more about what can we
do if we collaborate?

00:04:44.316 --> 00:04:45.784
What can we make together?

00:04:45.784 --> 00:04:48.854
And so people start projects and
they join each other's projects,

00:04:48.854 --> 00:04:51.223
and they build on each other,
and they remix each other

00:04:51.223 --> 00:04:53.392
and make all kinds
of cool things together.

00:04:53.392 --> 00:04:59.798
And that ended up being
this necessity for me last year.

00:04:59.798 --> 00:05:04.203
I was stuck inside and trying
to keep my head straight,

00:05:04.203 --> 00:05:06.472
isolating during the pandemic.

00:05:06.472 --> 00:05:09.309
And just doing
something creative

00:05:09.309 --> 00:05:10.710
and getting to do it
collaboratively

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:12.511
with other people
all over the world

00:05:12.511 --> 00:05:14.246
helped me feel connected
with other people

00:05:14.246 --> 00:05:15.848
in a real positive way,

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:17.616
helped me sometimes
take my mind off

00:05:17.616 --> 00:05:19.385
of the scary things
that were happening

00:05:19.385 --> 00:05:21.721
and just stay positive.

00:05:21.721 --> 00:05:23.122
But now I get to
come on your show

00:05:23.122 --> 00:05:25.090
and tell people about something
that I am doing.

00:05:25.090 --> 00:05:27.393
Like, we're making
this show today.

00:05:27.393 --> 00:05:29.896
You can got to HITRECORD
and get involved in projects.

00:05:29.896 --> 00:05:31.697
We're making the show right now.

00:05:31.697 --> 00:05:33.832
Anybody out there,
if you're an artist

00:05:33.832 --> 00:05:36.235
or even if you don't really
consider yourself an artist,

00:05:36.235 --> 00:05:38.537
there's lots of little
creative prompts.

00:05:38.537 --> 00:05:40.773
Even if you're not, like,
super skilled or practiced,

00:05:40.773 --> 00:05:42.574
you can just dip your toe
and get started.

00:05:42.574 --> 00:05:44.543
Like, that's a lot of the point
of it for me.

00:05:44.543 --> 00:05:47.579
It's not about
who can be the greatest artist.

00:05:47.579 --> 00:05:49.749
It's about let's all
do this together.

00:05:49.749 --> 00:05:52.919
-Here's a peek at Season 2
of "Create Together."

00:05:52.919 --> 00:05:54.620
It's happening now. Take a look.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:56.789
-♪ Now let me see you
bless the water ♪

00:05:56.789 --> 00:05:58.958
♪ Like the water blesses you ♪

00:05:58.958 --> 00:06:03.428 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:03.428 --> 00:06:04.697
-I'm going to sing on the show.

00:06:04.697 --> 00:06:07.433
I want you to come along,
sing with me.

00:06:07.433 --> 00:06:12.471 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:12.471 --> 00:06:13.773
-Go.

00:06:13.773 --> 00:06:18.710 line:0%
♪♪

00:06:18.710 --> 00:06:19.812 line:0%
[ Groundhog whistles ]

00:06:19.812 --> 00:06:21.146
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:21.146 --> 00:06:22.381
-Bud, that's so great.

00:06:22.381 --> 00:06:23.582
Congrats again.

00:06:23.582 --> 00:06:25.517
Joseph Gordon-Levitt!
-Thank you, man.

00:06:25.517 --> 00:06:26.552
Thank you, thank you.

